      "image": "/slides/ids_ids_ids_5_ids_5_svm_pdf/slide_003.webp",
      "thumb": "/slides/ids_ids_ids_5_ids_5_svm_pdf/thumb_003.webp",
      "text": "1. Maximum Margin\r\n- We always create a hyperplane that has a maximum margin, which means the maximum\r\ndistance between the data points.\r\n2. Support Vectors\r\n- The data points or vectors that are the closest to the hyperplane and which affect the\r\nposition of the hyperplane are termed as Support Vectors.\r\n3. Why are they called Support Vectors?\r\n- Since these vectors support the hyperplane, hence called a Support Vector.",
      "width": 1584,
      "height": 1224,
      "rects": [
        {
          "l": 3.49,
          "t": 22.01,
          "w": 20.14,
          "h": 2.7,
