          "h": 2.21,
          "text": "1. Linear SVM"
        },
        {
          "l": 17.83,
          "t": 33.68,
          "w": 78.35,
          "h": 2.82,
          "text": ": Linear SVM is used for linearly separable data, which means if a dataset can"
        },
        {
          "l": 3.37,
          "t": 39.5,
          "w": 92.89,
          "h": 2.82,
          "text": "be classified into two classes by using a single straight line, then such data is termed as"
        },
        {
          "l": 3.37,
          "t": 45.32,
          "w": 53.86,
          "h": 2.82,
          "text": "linearly separable data, and classifier used is called as "
        },
        {
          "l": 58.07,
          "t": 45.32,
